VALUES (4900932006070125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain JDBC connectivity model in the context of JDBC Programming. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain J2EE architecture in the context of J2EE Architecture, Servlets and JSP. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Sessions in the context of Enterprise Web Components. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Java networking in the context of Java Networking and Remote Method Invocation. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** JDBC connectivity model appears in “JDBC Programming”. Define its role and features, relate it to connecting to databases, creating SQL queries, retrieving query results, updating database data, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to connecting to databases, creating SQL queries, retrieving query results, updating database data, error checking. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Advance Java task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** J2EE architecture appears in “J2EE Architecture, Servlets and JSP”. Define its role and features, relate it to multi tier applications, MVC framework, network protocols, Servlet API, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to multi tier applications, MVC framework, network protocols, Servlet API, JSP API. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Advance Java task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Sessions appears in “Enterprise Web Components”. Define its role and features, relate it to filters, JSTL, JavaBeans, servlet processing, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to filters, JSTL, JavaBeans, servlet processing, JSP pages. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Advance Java task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Java networking appears in “Java Networking and Remote Method Invocation”. Define its role and features, relate it to remote method invocation RMI, client server communication, Java Networking and Remote Method Invocation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to remote method invocation RMI, client server communication, Java Networking and Remote Method Invocation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Advance Java task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

