VALUES (4900932006050135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Introduction of cloud computing in Cloud Computing. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving IAM Overview and Policies in Cloud Computing. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving What is Virtualization in Cloud Computing. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a realistic task involving Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS) in Cloud Computing. Explain the governing principle, justify the method or selection, and include a verification check and limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction of cloud computing appears in “Introduction of Cloud & Amazon Web Service”. Define its role and features, relate it to What is Virtualization, Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS), Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to What is Virtualization, Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS), Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), Advantages of Cloud. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cloud Computing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IAM Overview and Policies appears in “Identity & Access Management”. Define its role and features, relate it to IAM Users, Groups, Access Key & Secret Access Key, MFA, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to IAM Users, Groups, Access Key & Secret Access Key, MFA, Report. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cloud Computing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** What is Virtualization appears in “Introduction of Cloud & Amazon Web Service”. Define its role and features, relate it to Introduction of cloud computing, Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS), Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Introduction of cloud computing, Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS), Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), Advantages of Cloud. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cloud Computing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Infrastructure as a Service(IaaS) appears in “Introduction of Cloud & Amazon Web Service”. Define its role and features, relate it to Introduction of cloud computing, What is Virtualization, Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Introduction of cloud computing, What is Virtualization, Software as a Service(Saas), Platform as a Service(PaaS), Advantages of Cloud. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cloud Computing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

