: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Digital Differential Analyzer DDA line drawing appears in “Scan Conversion and Clipping”. Define its role and features, relate it to Bresenham line drawing, Bresenham circle drawing, midpoint circle algorithm, midpoint ellipse algorithm, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Bresenham line drawing, Bresenham circle drawing, midpoint circle algorithm, midpoint ellipse algorithm, aliasing. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** input devices appears in “Introduction to Computer Graphics”. Define its role and features, relate it to Overview of computer graphics, computer graphics applications, graphics software, graphics devices, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Overview of computer graphics, computer graphics applications, graphics software, graphics devices, active and passive graphics devices. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** active and passive graphics devices appears in “Introduction to Computer Graphics”. Define its role and features, relate it to Overview of computer graphics, computer graphics applications, graphics software, graphics devices, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Overview of computer graphics, computer graphics applications, graphics software, graphics devices, input devices. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

