VALUES (4900932006120130, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Computer Graphics & Animation involves the syllabus topic d transformations as applied within 2D and 3D Transformations, Viewing and Rendering. Explain how D transformations applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Computer Graphics & Animation involves the syllabus topic curve representation as applied within Curves and Surfaces. Explain how Curve representation applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Computer Graphics & Animation involves the syllabus topic principles of animation as applied within Computer Animation and Image Processing. Explain how Principles of animation applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Computer Graphics & Animation involves the syllabus topic computer graphics applications as applied within Introduction to Computer Graphics. Explain how computer graphics applications applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** D transformations appears in “2D and 3D Transformations, Viewing and Rendering”. Define its role and features, relate it to transformation matrices, homogeneous coordinates, translation, rotation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to transformation matrices, homogeneous coordinates, translation, rotation, reflection. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Curve representation appears in “Curves and Surfaces”. Define its role and features, relate it to non parametric curves, parametric curves, circle representation, ellipse representation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to non parametric curves, parametric curves, circle representation, ellipse representation, parabola representation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Principles of animation appears in “Computer Animation and Image Processing”. Define its role and features, relate it to key framing, deformations, character animation, physics based animation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to key framing, deformations, character animation, physics based animation, procedural techniques. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** computer graphics applications appears in “Introduction to Computer Graphics”. Define its role and features, relate it to Overview of computer graphics, graphics software, graphics devices, input devices, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Overview of computer graphics, graphics software, graphics devices, input devices, active and passive graphics devices. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Computer Graphics & Animation task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

