el answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Criminal organizations appears in “Introduction and Security Threats”. Define its role and features, relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Terrorists, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Terrorists, Information warfare Avenues of Attack. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Terrorists appears in “Introduction and Security Threats”. Define its role and features, relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Criminal organizations, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Criminal organizations, Information warfare Avenues of Attack. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Information warfare Avenues of Attack appears in “Introduction and Security Threats”. Define its role and features, relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Criminal organizations, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Intruders, Insiders, Criminal organizations, Terrorists. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

