VALUES (4900932006100130, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cyber Security involves the syllabus topic overview of ip security (ipsec) as applied within IP Security. Explain how Overview of IP Security (IPSec) applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cyber Security involves the syllabus topic web security requirements as applied within Web Security. Explain how Web Security Requirements applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cyber Security involves the syllabus topic ieee 802.11 as applied within Wireless Network Security Standards. Explain how IEEE 802.11 applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cyber Security involves the syllabus topic intruders as applied within Introduction and Security Threats. Explain how Intruders applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Overview of IP Security (IPSec) appears in “IP Security”. Define its role and features, relate it to IP Security Architecture, Modes of Operation, Security Associations (SA) Security Parameter Index (SPI), SA Management, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to IP Security Architecture, Modes of Operation, Security Associations (SA) Security Parameter Index (SPI), SA Management, Security Policy. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Web Security Requirements appears in “Web Security”. Define its role and features, relate it to Secure Socket Layer (SSL) SSL Architecture, SSL Protocol, Transport Layer Security (TLS), Secure Electronic Transaction (SET) Features, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Secure Socket Layer (SSL) SSL Architecture, SSL Protocol, Transport Layer Security (TLS), Secure Electronic Transaction (SET) Features, Components. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IEEE 802.11 appears in “Wireless Network Security Standards”. Define its role and features, relate it to IEEE 802.11i Wireless LAN Security, WAP protocol, WAP End-to-End Security Total 43 hrs, Wireless Network Security Standards, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to IEEE 802.11i Wireless LAN Security, WAP protocol, WAP End-to-End Security Total 43 hrs, Wireless Network Security Standards. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Intruders appears in “Introduction and Security Threats”. Define its role and features, relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Insiders, Criminal organizations, Terrorists, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Threats to security: Viruses and Worms, Insiders, Criminal organizations, Terrorists, Information warfare Avenues of Attack. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cyber Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

