VALUES (4900932006030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Embedded Systems involves the syllabus topic embedded systems as applied within Introduction to Embedded Systems. Explain how Embedded Systems applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Embedded Systems involves the syllabus topic microcontrollers and embedded processors as applied within AVR microcontroller-History and Features. Explain how Microcontrollers and embedded processors applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Embedded Systems involves the syllabus topic programming: general purpose registers in avr as applied within AVR Microcontroller Architecture and assembly language. Explain how programming: General Purpose registers in AVR applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Embedded Systems involves the syllabus topic data types and time delay in c as applied within AVR programming in C. Explain how Data types and time delay in C applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Embedded Systems appears in “Introduction to Embedded Systems”. Define its role and features, relate it to Processor Embedded into a System, Embedded Hardware Units and Devices In a System, Embedded Software in a system, Examples of Embedded Systems, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Processor Embedded into a System, Embedded Hardware Units and Devices In a System, Embedded Software in a system, Examples of Embedded Systems, Embedded System-on-chip (SOC) and Use of VLSI Circuit Design Technology. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Embedded Systems task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Microcontrollers and embedded processors appears in “AVR microcontroller-History and Features”. Define its role and features, relate it to Criteria for choosing a microcontroller, Simplified view of AVR microcontroller, ATMega32 block diagram, Overview of AVR family Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Criteria for choosing a microcontroller, Simplified view of AVR microcontroller, ATMega32 block diagram, Overview of AVR family Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, AVR microcontroller-History and Features. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Embedded Systems task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** programming: General Purpose registers in AVR appears in “AVR Microcontroller Architecture and assembly language”. Define its role and features, relate it to The AVR data memory, AVR status register, AVR data formats and assembler directives, Assembly Language Programming, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to The AVR data memory, AVR status register, AVR data formats and assembler directives, Assembly Language Programming, Program Counter and program ROM space in AVR. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Embedded Systems task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Data types and time delay in C appears in “AVR programming in C”. Define its role and features, relate it to I/O port programming in C, Logic operations in C, Data conversion programs in C, Data serialization in C, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to I/O port programming in C, Logic operations in C, Data conversion programs in C, Data serialization in C, Memory allocation in C. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Embedded Systems task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

