-- RF and Microwave Communication | ESE | easy | 4900932006040125 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4900932006040125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain History of Microwaves in the context of Introduction to Microwaves. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Concept of Mode in the context of Mathematical model of Microwave Transmission. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Transmission line equations & solutions in the context of Analysis of Microwave Transmission Lines and Waveguides. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Equivalent voltages and currents for non-TEM lines in the context of Microwave Network Analysis. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** History of Microwaves appears in “Introduction to Microwaves”. Define its role and features, relate it to Microwave frequency bands, General applications of Microwaves, Advantages of Microwaves, Microwave Propagation, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Microwave frequency bands, General applications of Microwaves, Advantages of Microwaves, Microwave Propagation, Introduction to Microwaves. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept of Mode appears in “Mathematical model of Microwave Transmission”. Define its role and features, relate it to Characteristics of TEM, TE and TM Modes, Losses associated with microwave transmission, Concept of Impedance in Microwave transmission Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of TEM, TE and TM Modes, Losses associated with microwave transmission, Concept of Impedance in Microwave transmission Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, Mathematical model of Microwave Transmission. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Transmission line equations & solutions appears in “Analysis of Microwave Transmission Lines and Waveguides”. Define its role and features, relate it to reflection and transmission coefficient, standing wave and standing wave ratio, line impedance and admittance, impedance matching, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to reflection and transmission coefficient, standing wave and standing wave ratio, line impedance and admittance, impedance matching, using stub line. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Equivalent voltages and currents for non-TEM lines appears in “Microwave Network Analysis”. Define its role and features, relate it to Network parameters for microwave circuits, Scattering Parameters, Microwave Network Analysis, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Network parameters for microwave circuits, Scattering Parameters, Microwave Network Analysis. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

