fety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concept of Mode appears in “Mathematical model of Microwave Transmission”. Define its role and features, relate it to Characteristics of TEM, TE and TM Modes, Losses associated with microwave transmission, Concept of Impedance in Microwave transmission Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of TEM, TE and TM Modes, Losses associated with microwave transmission, Concept of Impedance in Microwave transmission Marwadi University Faculty of Diploma studies Information and Communication Technology, Mathematical model of Microwave Transmission. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete RF and Microwave Communication task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Transmission line equations & solutions appears in “Analysis of Microwave Transmission Lines and Waveguides”. Define its role and features, relate it to reflection and transmission coefficient, standing wave and standing wave ratio, line impedance and admittance, impedance matching, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm th