VALUES (4900932006080125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Definitions in the context of Introduction to Internet of Things. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Working principles in the context of Sensors. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Bluetooth and BLE in the context of Communication devices and protocols. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain with interoperable data encoding with XML in the context of Application layer: MQTT, CoAP, XMPP, Integrating internet services. Define it, describe the key principles or steps, and give one relevant practical example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definitions appears in “Introduction to Internet of Things”. Define its role and features, relate it to core concepts, related concepts, IoT reference models, IoT architectures, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to core concepts, related concepts, IoT reference models, IoT architectures, challenges. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Sensor and IoT (SIoT) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Working principles appears in “Sensors”. Define its role and features, relate it to different types, selection of sensors for practical applications, Introduction to different types of sensors such as capacitive, resistive, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to different types, selection of sensors for practical applications, Introduction to different types of sensors such as capacitive, resistive, temperature. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Sensor and IoT (SIoT) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Bluetooth and BLE appears in “Communication devices and protocols”. Define its role and features, relate it to Wifi, Zigbee, IPv6, LowPAN, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Wifi, Zigbee, IPv6, LowPAN, LTE-M. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Sensor and IoT (SIoT) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** with interoperable data encoding with XML appears in “Application layer: MQTT, CoAP, XMPP, Integrating internet services”. Define its role and features, relate it to JSON, CBOR, sensor markup language, lightweight web services for IoT, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to JSON, CBOR, sensor markup language, lightweight web services for IoT, Application layer: MQTT, CoAP, XMPP, Integrating internet services. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Sensor and IoT (SIoT) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

