ing and purpose (2 marks):** Services and Features appears in “Global System for Mobile Communications (GSM)”. Define its role and features, relate it to System Architecture, Radio sub systems, Channel types, Example of a GSM call, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to System Architecture, Radio sub systems, Channel types, Example of a GSM call, Frame Structure. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Microcell zone concept appears in “Introduction to Cellular Communication”. Define its role and features, relate it to Cellular cell concepts: cell structure, frequency reuse, cell splitting, cell sectoring, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Cellular cell concepts: cell structure, frequency reuse, cell splitting, cell sectoring, channel assignment. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarki