ion, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Stack appears in “Wireless Personal Area Networks: Bluetooth Specifications, Protocols”. Define its role and features, relate it to Security Issues, Advantages and Disadvantages, Application, UWB, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Security Issues, Advantages and Disadvantages, Application, UWB, Zigbee. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** NFC appears in “GPS, wireless local loop, cordless phone, paging systems, RFID, Home RF,”. Define its role and features, relate it to Software Defined Radio, Wireless Sensor Networks, Security issues and challenges in wireless networks Total 42 hrs., GPS, wireless local loop, cordless phone, paging systems, RFID, Home RF,, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Software Defined Radio, Wireless Sensor Networks, Security issues and challenges in wireless networks Total 42 hrs., GPS, wireless local loop, cordless phone, paging systems, RFID, Home RF,. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** frequency reuse appears in “Introduction to Cellular Communication”. Define its role and features, relate it to Cellular cell concepts: cell structure, cell splitting, cell sectoring, Microcell zone concept, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Cellular cell concepts: cell structure, cell splitting, cell sectoring, Microcell zone concept, channel assignment. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Wireless Technologies task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

